Conditional hashing is a concept where you compute a hash only if certain conditions are met, or compute different hashes based on different conditions.
Real-World Use Cases
✔ Deduplication systems: Hash file only if size > X MB (to avoid overhead).
✔ Authentication systems: Hash only after checking password complexity rules or version.
✔ Distributed systems:Use a different hash function based on: Key type, Version and Partitioning scheme
Why Conditional Hashing Exists
- Improve performance: Reduce unnecessary hashing
- Support variable data formats

