-> CDN (Content Delivery Network) is a globally distributed network of servers that delivers content (images, videos, scripts, APIs, files) fast, reliably, and close to users.
A network of geographically spread-out “mini-copies” of your website or content that users load from the closest location.
When a user requests a resource: User hits the nearest CDN edge server (not your origin server). If content exists in cache → served instantly.
If not → CDN pulls it from your origin server, caches it, then serves it. Future users get it instantly from cache.
🏢 Common CDNs Used in Industry: Cloudflare, Akamai

-> Proxy: A server that sits between the client and the internet. It forwards your requests for you.
Uses: Hide your IP, Bypass geo-restrictions and Filter/block websites (corporate/college proxy)

-> Load Bal: A load balancer is a component that distributes incoming traffic across multiple backend servers to prevent overload and ensure high availability.
What it does: Spreads requests evenly across servers, Removes unhealthy servers from rotation, Ensures zero downtime during deploys (blue-green, rolling), Helps your app scale horizontally
NGINX / HAProxy

-> Gateway: An API Gateway is a smart, centralized entry point for all API traffic that adds security, routing, rate-limiting, and transformations before requests reach your microservices.
What it does: Authentication (JWT, OAuth), Rate limiting / throttling, Request/response transformation, Routing to multiple internal services
NGINX as gateway

-> VPN: A VPN creates an encrypted, private tunnel between your device and a VPN server, so all your internet traffic is secure and your IP is hidden.
NordVPN

Remove CDN: Backend gets overloaded serving images/files; global users face high latency.
Remove LB: Only one server gets traffic; no horizontal scaling; single point of failure.
Remove Gateway: Each microservice must handle auth, rate limits, CORS, logging → messy architecture.
Remove VPN: Internal systems become exposed; security risk.
Remove Proxy: Usually no issue unless you rely on it for filtering / routing.

